\n- Use the configured trailing release window without mixing epochs.\\n- Project the candidate release without writing a ledger row.\\n- Compare the candidate projection with the durable release target.\\n- Compare PR-time impact with the no-op base projection.\\n- Add real session-backed work when the candidate would lower the share.\\n\\n## 5. Keep retries idempotent\\n\\n- Exclude an existing row for the tag from its own retry projection.\\n- Accept a repeated release record only when every field is identical.\\n- Reject duplicate tag rows that disagree with committed history.\\n- Leave version files unchanged until eligibility succeeds.\\n- Re-run the same precondition after fetching newer tags or main commits.\\n- Preserve the open release range when more reviewed work is required.\\n\\n## 6. Preserve existing trust gates\\n\\n- Do not grant Formal AI merge, approval, or promotion authority.\\n- Send authored bytes through ordinary human review.\\n- Require the same CI matrix used for other repository changes.\\n- Keep trusted promotion rules in force for learned runtime behavior.\\n- Treat the release gate as evidence verification, not authorization.\\n- Record failures without bypassing branch protection.\\n\\n## 7. Validate before version mutation\\n\\n- Run the self-development release gate before editing Cargo metadata.\\n- Confirm a qualifying reviewed PR exists in the current release range.\\n- Confirm the projected share meets the non-decreasing target.\\n- Confirm the working tree is clean before automated version changes.\\n- Abort without partial edits when any precondition fails.\\n- Re-run after remediation instead of increasing a timeout or threshold.\\n\\n## 8. Record the successful release\\n\\n- Store the release tag, range endpoints, and canonical until commit.\\n- Store authored and total changed-line counts.\\n- Store authored and total non-merge commit counts.\\n- Store the per-release and trailing percentages.\\n- Store the target that governed the release.\\n- Store every qualifying Formal AI-authored pull-request URL.\\n\\n## 9. Publish reviewable evidence\\n\\n- Include the self-hosting share in generated release notes.\\n- Include the trailing share and non-decreasing target.\\n- Link the reviewed pull requests that satisfied the release floor.\\n- Preserve raw Agent CLI output for replay and audit.\\n- Preserve the Formal AI server trace for the recorded session.\\n- Keep the exact authored artifact beside its evidence bundle.\\n\\n## 10. Investigate a red ratchet\\n\\n- Verify the run used the newest commit and release tag.\\n- Compare timestamps and head SHA before diagnosing stale CI data.\\n- Preserve the complete failed workflow log locally.\\n- Find the exact numerator and denominator behind both projections.\\n- Attribute only work actually produced by a recorded Formal AI session.\\n- Split unrelated work instead of weakening the target.\\n\\n## 11. Finalize the pull request\\n\\n- Merge the latest default branch and resolve generated-file drift.\\n- Run focused regressions before the full local CI-equivalent suite.\\n- Verify strict lint, examples, policies, and derived artifacts.\\n- Push only the prepared issue branch.\\n- Confirm every required check belongs to the pushed head SHA.\\n- Mark the pull request ready only after all required checks pass.\\n\\nCompletion means the release contains real Formal AI work whose unchanged\\nbytes passed normal review, CI, promotion rules, and the self-hosting ratchet.\"\n    command \"cat docs/case-studies/issue-924/v0343-ratchet-authorship/release-checklist.md\"\n  verification_command \"cat docs/case-studies/issue-924/v0343-ratchet-authorship/release-checklist.md\"\n","filePath":".formal-ai/general-change-plan.lino","file_path":".formal-ai/general-change-plan.lino","path":".formal-ai/general-change-plan.lino"} emitted={"content":"general_change_plan\n  id \"general_change_plan_814813c8682f9d5d\"\n  execution_mode \"literal_file\"\n  terminal_